Frequency lists compiled from the observed light curves, used to test the Freqdiag programme

\rrab_bl_kepler <- Kepler Blazho RRab stars from Benko et al. (2014, ApJS 213, id.31); 
                   freqlists* are generated by lc_multi.py (block-based pre-whitening and LS amplitude spectra)

Typical run:

./freqdiag.py NAME   --separator whitespace  \
 --no-header --skiprows 5 \
 --freq-col 2   --amp-col 4  --phase-col 6   --phase-convention cosine --phase-unit cycles \
 --baseline 1440   --nmax 20  \
 --lmax-modulation 3   --lmax-coupling 3   --outdir "diag_"NAME

 
\rrc_tess_cvz   <- TESS RRc stars from Benko et al. (2023, MNRAS 521, 443)
                   freqlists* are generated by lc_multi.py (block-based pre-whitening and LS amplitude spectra)

Typical run:

./freqdiag.py NAME   --separator whitespace  \
 --no-header --skiprows 5 \
 --freq-col 2   --amp-col 4  --phase-col 6   --phase-convention cosine --phase-unit cycles \
 --baseline 350   --nmax 20  \
 --lmax-modulation 3   --lmax-coupling 3   --outdir "diag_"NAME

\rrab_bl_k2     <- 10 K2 Blazhko RRab stars
\rrc_bl_k2      <- 10 K2 Blazhko RRc stars
                   *.freqs files are generated by Seisnolab tool (Bodi 2024, The Journal of Open Source Software 9, 7118)

Typical run:

./freqdiag.py NAME   --separator whitespace   --no-header \
 --freq-col 1   --amp-col 2   --phase-col 3   --phase-unit rad \
 --baseline 90   --nmax 20  \
 --lmax-modulation 3   --lmax-coupling 3   --outdir "diag_"NAME
